      "feel" : "required",
      "group" : "output",
      "binding" : {
        "key" : "resultExpression",
        "type" : "zeebe:taskHeader"
      },
      "tooltip" : "Maps the response into process variables, and the shape differs per operation. Execute statement returns status.state plus result.data_array, Run job now returns run_id, Get run returns state.life_cycle_state and state.result_state, and chat returns choices, where FEEL lists are 1-indexed. See <a href=\"https://docs.camunda.io/docs/components/connectors/use-connectors/#result-expression\">result expression</a>.",
      "type" : "Text"
    },
    {
      "id" : "errorExpression",
      "label" : "Error expression",
      "description" : "Note: a failed SQL statement returns HTTP 200 with status.state FAILED, so the status code alone does not indicate success.",
      "value" : "=if response != null and response.body != null and response.body.status != null and response.body.status.state != null and (response.body.status.state = \"FAILED\" or response.body.status.state = \"CANCELED\" or response.body.status.state = \"CLOSED\") then bpmnError(\"DATABRICKS_SQL_\" + response.body.status.state, \"Databricks SQL statement ended in state \" + response.body.status.state + \": \" + (if response.body.status.error = null then \"no error detail returned\" else response.body.status.error.message)) else null",
      "feel" : "required",
      "group" : "error",
